## fig-78

Source: ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/8a/figures/fig-78.png
SHA256 f44be5c7a41bba37856b14f1ea7199e4511913fa735448f65bbcd567aac3c55e

78-left-scale: one left horizontal number line, directed right. Five upward
ticks labelled -3,-2,-1,0,1 from left to right, equally spaced.
78-left-integer: x above the -2 tick, [x]=x below the line. There is NO left
downward arrow. The short vertical stroke under x is the upward axis tick.
There is no separately printed dot or hollow point.
78-right-scale: a separate right horizontal number line directed right,
also labelled -3,-2,-1,0,1 at equally spaced upward ticks.
78-right-noninteger: [x] above -1, [x]+1 above 0, and x above a genuine
downward pointer ending strictly between those ticks. The source supplies
no exact fractional value for x; do not print or treat one as a given.
There is no rectangular grid, additional axis name or extra subfigure.

Planned stable IDs: 78-left-tick-m3/m2/m1/z0/p1 and
78-right-tick-m3/m2/m1/z0/p1; 78-left-x; 78-left-floor;
78-right-x; 78-right-pointer-top; 78-right-floor-label;
78-right-successor-label; number-line arrows and tick segments inherit
the relevant scale ID. Each mapped point must have a displacement,
coincidence, collinearity or connects relation inside its inventory group.

## fig-79

Source: ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/8a/figures/fig-79.png
SHA256 69b75de07afccdaef626fb2c192059736a2db32e45fb76ef022d9ddc38453174

79-lattice: one square frame. Counted 19 native lines each way, hence
exactly 18 columns and 18 rows. Consecutive labelled integers are separated
by two cells: cell size is 0.5 in each coordinate.
79-frame-origin: the vertical axis is the eighth grid line from the left
(seven cells from the left); the horizontal axis is the tenth line from
the top (nine cells from the top). Thus x=-3.5..5.5, y=-4.5..4.5.
79-axes: rightward positive x arrow, upward positive y arrow, labels x/y.
The source origin label is italic O, not numerical zero.
79-x-labels: -2,-1,O,1,2,3. Labels lie below the horizontal axis.
79-y-labels: -2,-1,1,2. The two negative labels are right of the vertical
axis; the two positive labels are left of it.
79-piece-m2: (-2,-2) -> (-1,-2).
79-piece-m1: (-1,-1) -> (0,-1).
79-piece-z0: (0,0) -> (1,0), overlapping the horizontal axis.
79-piece-p1: (1,1) -> (2,1).
79-piece-p2: (2,2) -> (3,2).
All FIVE right endpoints have hollow circles. Left endpoints are line
starts with NO hollow circles and NO separately printed filled dots.
No vertical jumps, extra graph sections, dashed curves or arbitrary point
names are present.

Each piece ID will own -left/-right point IDs, a -segment, -span assertion,
and -connection assertion, wholly mapped in its own pointRelationships
inventory group. The lattice group requires gridDimensions, not objectCount.

## fig-80

Source: ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/8a/figures/fig-80.png
SHA256 372066296f2cf94ed290eb892765ef38e670b350a9b5418f2867e4f0be815742

80-lattice: one square frame, 19 native lines each way: 18 columns and
18 rows, 0.5 units per cell.
80-frame-origin: nine cells from left, eleven from top. Thus x=-4.5..4.5,
y=-3.5..5.5.
80-axes: positive arrows right/up, labels x/y, italic O at the origin.
80-x-labels: -3,-2,-1,O,1,2,3 below the horizontal axis.
80-y-labels: 1,2,3 to the left of the vertical axis.
80-piece-m3: (-3,0) -> (-2,1).
80-piece-m2: (-2,0) -> (-1,1).
80-piece-m1: (-1,0) -> (0,1).
80-piece-z0: (0,0) -> (1,1).
80-piece-p1: (1,0) -> (2,1).
80-piece-p2: (2,0) -> (3,1).
All SIX upper-right endpoints are hollow. All lower-left starts meet
y=0 without hollow circles or separately printed filled dots.
No vertical reset connections or extension beyond these six segments.
Each piece will receive the same fully mapped endpoint relation coverage
as 79, with displacement (1,1) rather than (1,0).

## Deliberate modern decisions, NOT original pixel facts

Use deterministic JSXGraph geometry, semantic colors and readable labels.
Keep both 78 number lines separate. Their layout offsets and the right
pointer's particular interior placement are illustrative regularization,
not a newly supplied numerical x value.
For 79/80 add small filled LEFT endpoint indicators solely to make the
authoritative [n,n+1[ inclusion convention explicit. Preserve hollow RIGHT
endpoint indicators. These filled dots are additions, not printed source dots.
Use a mathematical italic O glyph for the original italic origin notation.
Do not add function-title labels, extra numerical ticks or graph sections.
Instructional display: scroll media at actual width 640px; target 22px
labels and enforce at least 16px. Scroll-end behavior must be measured
in the offline display test, not assumed from canvas dimensions.

